Browser connector
-----------------

The Plaud connector browser extension can sign in to Plaud and send the
resulting token to an OpenAudioHub instance. It is a separate project,
maintained at https://github.com/JeremyL691/openaudiohub-connector under
AGPL-3.0. This repository does not include its code.


Bundled and loaded third-party components
-----------------------------------------

- Silero VAD model, audio-pipeline/models/silero_vad.onnx.
  Copyright (c) 2020-present Silero Team. Licensed under the MIT License.
  The license text is in audio-pipeline/models/SILERO_LICENSE.txt.
  Upstream: https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad

- Geist and Geist Mono typefaces, loaded at build time through
  next/font/google. Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, version 1.1.
  Upstream: https://github.com/vercel/geist-font

- Components of the Mac app: Electron (which includes Node.js and Chromium),
  PostgreSQL 16, ffmpeg, libopus and LAME (built from source with the LGPL
  configuration), and the Python runtime of the audio pipeline with its locked
  wheels. The Mac app bundle has a THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md file that lists each
  of these components with its license, and a licenses folder with the license
  files that the upstream packages provide. Both are inside
  OpenAudioHub.app under Contents/Resources, including the Silero VAD model's
  license (audio-pipeline/models/SILERO_LICENSE.txt in this repository).

Other dependencies are listed in package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml,
audio-pipeline/pyproject.toml, and uv.lock. Their licenses are carried by
the packages themselves.


